===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of the [[physical]] [[sense]]s or [[sensation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|1665|author=<!-- anonymous translator -->|title=Bartholinus Anatomy|location=London|publisher=Nich. Culpeper and Abdiah Cole|chapter=VI|type=translation|original=Anatomia|by={{w|Thomas Bartholin}}|seriesvolume=book III|page=142|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/2306045R.nlm.nih.gov/2306045R#page/n156|passage=The Species of things are perceived rather there whereto they are carried. But every '''ſenſory''' Nerve each in its place carries the Species to the beginning of the ſpinal Marrow, and therefore each in their place are judged and received by the Soul, in the beginning of the ſpinal Marrow.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1873|{{w|Alpheus Spring Packard}}|chapter=Hints on the Ancestry of Insects|Our Common Insects: A Popular Account of the Insects of Our Fields, Forests, Gardens and Houses|location=Salem|publisher=Naturalists’ Agency|page=174|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dIpIAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA174|passage=It is evident that in the ancestor of these two groups the first pair of appendages became early adapted for purely '''sensory''' purposes, and were naturally projected far in advance of the mouth, forming the antennæ.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|1991|Tetsuo Matsui|author2=Susumu Kato|author3=Susan E. Smith|Biology and Potential Use of Pacific Grenadier, ''Coryphaenoides acrolepis'', off California|Marine Fisheries Review|volume=52|number=3|issn=0090-1830|http://aquaticcommons.org/9929|13|Findings of the '''sensory''' analysis panel at NWFSC [the {{w|Northwest Fisheries Science Center}}], which tested and classified flesh characteristics of both Pacific and giant grenadier, are averaged and summarized in Table 10.}}
# {{lb|en|neuroanatomy}} [[convey|Convey]]ing [[nerve impulse]]s from the [[sense organ]]s to the [[nerve center]]s.
#: {{ux|en|'''sensory''' neurons}}
#: {{syn|en|afferent}}

